id: pm-csv-yriu
title: Test wrapper lets delegated writers outlive buffer-overrun teardown
description: "The original ENOTEMPTY cleanup retry is shipped, but it does not establish writer lifetime. spawnSync waits for its direct child; when that child is the transparent test wrapper, a tiny outer output cap can kill the wrapper while its real pm descendant continues closing an item. Removing the temporary tracker can then race a history open and report an unintended CI fault through production observability. A real-process regression reproduces the surviving descendant. The corrected wrapper waits for real pm to exit before forwarding bounded captured output, and negative subprocess fixtures use an isolated global tracker with explicit observability opt-outs. The cleanup retry remains bounded for transient removal faults and its documentation now distinguishes child reaping from directory removal."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T20:20:17.350Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-06T18:14:09.188Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-06T18:14:08.801Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-06T18:14:08.801Z"
author: codex
resolution: "Capture delegated test-wrapper output until the real process exits, require real writer completion and reaping under an outer buffer overrun, and isolate global test state and observability."
expected_result: A test output overrun cannot let its real writer continue into fixture cleanup or emit a production incident.
actual_result: "Real-process regression is red before the fix and green after; Node 22.23.2 and Node 26.7.0 F2 acceptance passes, all 225 tests pass at exact 100 percent coverage, static gates and three linked plans pass."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-06T18:02:27.017Z",codex,"Release-unblocking investigation: the completed retrying-cleanup fix is present, but the transparent test wrapper still spawns real pm with inherited output. An outer 16-byte capture can terminate the wrapper while its descendant writes history. Reusing this canonical cleanup owner after a complete 96-item all-status census; no duplicate created. PM-CLI-3A has one CI Node 22 event at the F2 test boundary and no later recurrence. Exact fixture reproduction and lifetime prevention are required; this correlation is not yet definitive event attribution. Related release evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1209 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-3lhth4.toon ."
  "2026-09-06T18:05:53.711Z",codex,"TDD evidence: the new real-process regression failed against the inherited-output wrapper because the delegated writer was still active when the outer 16-byte capture returned ENOBUFS. No filesystem errors or process results were mocked. The corrected wrapper captures its child output until exit before forwarding it, so the same regression can require the completion marker and ESRCH for the reaped PID. Negative fixtures now inherit a disposable global tracker and explicit Sentry/telemetry opt-outs before SDK imports."
  "2026-09-06T18:14:08.371Z",codex,"Verification: the original real-process lifetime negative control failed; the corrected wrapper and exact F2 fixture pass on Node 26.7.0 and Node 22.23.2. All 225 tests pass with exact 100 percent source lines, branches and functions; typecheck, test typecheck, ESLint, duplicate gate, docstrings, production audit, package dry run and all three linked tests pass. The unmodified F2 scenario did not reproduce its historical ENOENT on this machine, so the historical event remains an attribution inference from matching runtime, timing and call path; the demonstrated descendant lifetime defect is independently fixed. No external error capture ran during these negative controls."
